# Line-ending policy.
#
# `scripts/verify.sh` is invoked as `bash scripts/verify.sh`. With
# `core.autocrlf=true` and no attributes, Git checked it out CRLF, so bash on
# this machine (WSL at C:\Windows\System32\bash.exe) parsed
# `set -euo pipefail\r` and died with
#   scripts/verify.sh: line 4: set: pipefail: invalid option name
# before running a single stage. Shell scripts must be LF in the working tree
# everywhere, so they are checked out and committed with LF regardless of the
# user's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
